{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1780363585,"nonce":"KRfM0tuUIueSiM9xbrL+CVF2c78=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABED_JEg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/202","origin":"github"},"title":"Write BizzyBoat operator manual (student-facing)","message":"## Summary\n\nWrite a **BizzyBoat operator manual** for student operators (rotating Summer Hydro\ncohorts): how to bring the boat up, drive it, run a survey, and shut it down — the\nproject11 autonomy layer on top of the boat, not the boat hardware itself.\n\nHardware and physical operation defer to the **EchoBoat 240 vendor manual**.\nLaunch/recovery is site-specific and intentionally out of scope here.\n\n## Outline\n\n1. **Overview \u0026 safety** — BizzyBoat (EchoBoat 240), uncrewed, RC-override-anytime; defer physical/hardware operation to the EchoBoat 240 manual\n2. **Readiness checks** — power state, battery charge (charged in place, no swap), GPS/NTRIP lock, comms link\n3. **Starting the stack** — power-on sequence, gabby/mercat roles, confirming the boat is up\n4. **Driving \u0026 autonomy** — manual joystick, Standby (→MANUAL / RC handoff), Hover, Goto, running a survey line, heartbeat-as-ack\n5. **Comms \u0026 range** — WiFi backhaul + Starlink/VPN fallback; OTH is normal; link drop is not an error\n6. **Shutdown \u0026 post-run**\n\nAlso reconcile the stale repo `README.md` (still describes IzzyBoat 160) to BizzyBoat 240.\n\n## Out of scope / cross-references\n\n- Engineer setup/deployment lives in the deployment guide (#18) — not duplicated here\n- \"How the autonomy stack works\" lives in a standalone framework guide (rolker/unh_marine_autonomy) — this manual links to it instead of carrying a symptom→cure troubleshooting section\n- No mission-specific (site/customer) detail\n\nRelated to #18.\n\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: ``\n**Model**: ``","files":null}]}